1. `Debug.Assert(New_Ret <= Old_arrListLastIndexOfX);`

The assertion checks if the return value (New_Ret) of the IndexOf method is less than or equal to the last index of x in the new list (Old_arrListLastIndexOfX). If it is, the program continues running; if it's not, the program will stop at that line. This assertion is likely to ensure that when a value is found in the list, the index given is the position of the last occurrence of that value in the list.
--------------------Based on the comments and the code provided, there are two assertions we should make:

1. After executing the `IndexOf` method, the return value is non-negative, it should be less than or equal to the last index of `x` in the new list. This suggests the following assertion:
   ```cs
   Debug.Assert(New_Ret <= New_arrListLastIndexOfX);
   ```

2. The count of the list before the `IndexOf` operation should be the same as the count of the list after the `IndexOf` operation. This suggests the following assertion:
   ```cs
   Debug.Assert(Old_arrListCount == New_arrListCount);
   ```

Here is the complete assertion code:

```cs
namespace ArrayList.Test
{
    public partial class ArrayListContractTest
    {
        public void PUT_IndexOfContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, int x)
        {
            AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(true);

            int Old_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
            int Old_x = x;
            int Old_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);
            bool Old_arrListContainsX = arrList.Contains(x);

            int New_Ret = arrList.IndexOf(x);

            int New_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
            int New_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);
            bool New_arrListContainsX = arrList.Contains(x);

            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$old_arrList_Count", Old_arrListCount);
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$new_arrList_Count", New_arrListCount);
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$old_arrList_x", Old_x);
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$old_arrList_LastIndexOf_x", Old_arrListLastIndexOfX);
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$new_arrList_LastIndexOf_x", New_arrListLastIndexOfX);
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$New_ret", New_Ret);
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$old_arrList_contains_x", Old_arrListContainsX);
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$new_arrList_contains_x", New_arrListContainsX);

            // @@@ If the return value is non-negative
            Debug.Assert(New_Ret >= 0);

            // @@@ If the return value is non-negative, new ret <= last index of x in new list
            Debug.Assert(New_Ret <= New_arrListLastIndexOfX);

            // @@@ Count of the list should remain the same before and after the operation
            Debug.Assert(Old_arrListCount == New_arrListCount);
        }
    }
}
```

This code adds three assertions at the end of the `PUT_IndexOfContract` method. The first one checks if the return value of the `IndexOf` method is non-negative. The second one checks if the return value is less than or equal to the last index of `x` in the new list. The third assertion checks if the count of the list before and after the `IndexOf` operation remains the same.
